voice check, read it against the script:
    Nod, a client just sent feedback, four emails, two voice notes, and a screenshot. Which version? Nobody knows. Tell them how you handle it. A spreadsheet, sticky notes, three hours of copy and paste. They want easy. Then show them. Watch. Step one, share the proof in her portal. Does she need an account? No, she clicks the work and comments. Even voice notes. Voice notes, video, arrows on the design. Step two, every comment becomes a task. With the pin. Right where she left it, assigned with the deadlines. Step three, she asks for something extra. Round five. It becomes a change order, she approves it, it lands on the invoice. Wait, can my team use this too? Yep, clients and freelancers you bring in are free, one price per studio. So I never chase feedback again. Less chasing, clients are still clients. So the problem was me. The problem was four inboxes.
